{"hash":"0a36d8593d6aefa4","voice":"en-IN-NeerjaExpressiveNeural","rate":"+4%","dur":75.925,"said":"You are in the sabha mandapa. Twenty-four carved pillars hold up its roof, and in the middle Nandi lies facing the sanctum, his eyes always on his Lord. Watch the men ahead of you in the line: they are taking off their shirts and vests before they go in. That is the custom here; men enter the sanctum bare-chested. And here is something only a few Jyotirlingas allow: at Grishneshwar, devotees may reach out and touch the linga, and pour water on it with their own hands. Remember Ghushma, who worshipped every day with her own hands, lingas she had shaped from the earth. Perhaps that is why it feels right that here, so little stands between the devotee and the Lord. Notice, too, that the sanctum lies lower than this hall. You will step down to it through a passage in the thick wall, and the linga faces east, toward Nandi and the morning sun. The day here is framed by worship: an aarti at dawn, the midday bhog, and the evening aarti. Go on now, and go down. This is the last step of a long journey.\n\nDid you know? The garbhagriha is about seventeen feet square, and its floor lies below the level of the hall.","segments":[{"key":"text","start":0,"end":1007},{"key":"didYouKnow","start":1023,"end":1118}],"words":[[0.098,0.228,0,3],[0.338,0.228,4,7],[0.579,0.096,8,10],[0.687,0.084,11,14],[0.783,0.385,15,20],[1.18,0.505,21,28],[2.584,0.529,30,41],[3.125,0.325,42,48],[3.462,0.421,49,56],[3.894,0.264,57,61],[4.171,0.156,62,64],[4.339,0.204,65,68],[4.555,0.397,69,73],[5.312,0.204,75,78],[5.529,0.084,79,81],[5.625,0.084,82,85],[5.721,0.349,86,92],[6.082,0.325,93,98],[6.418,0.3,99,103],[6.731,0.385,104,110],[7.127,0.096,111,114],[7.236,0.601,115,122],[8.077,0.156,124,127],[8.245,0.228,128,132],[8.486,0.433,133,139],[8.93,0.144,140,142],[9.087,0.18,143,146],[9.279,0.361,147,151],[10.517,0.3,153,158],[10.829,0.096,159,162],[10.938,0.3,163,166],[11.25,0.216,167,172],[11.478,0.168,173,1